  "solutions": {
    "36": "896 unit cubes. Multiply 16 by 7 by 8 to find the prism volume.",
    "37": "3/8 of the cake. The family takes half of the remaining 3/4, so multiply 1/2 by 3/4.",
    "38": "24 stickers per sheet. Divide 1,320 by 55.",
    "39": "5 1/4 inches. Add the lengths shown on the plot: 6(1/4) + 3(1/2) + 3(3/4) = 21/4.",
    "40": "8 3/4 square feet. Count 5 rows or columns of 7 tiles for 35 tiles. Each tile covers 1/4 square foot, so the area is 35/4 square feet.",
    "41": "Rosa. Steve has only 1/8 as many cards as Rosa, and 1/8 is less than 1.",
    "42": "362.408. The final digit represents eight thousandths. The final addend should be 8 x 1/1000.",
    "43": "84 more cubes. The prism holds 6 x 2 x 8 = 96 cubes. The base already contains 6 x 2 = 12 cubes. Subtract to get 84.",
    "44": "$103.50. The fabric costs 18 x $6.75 = $121.50. The fabric makes 18 / 1.5 = 12 blankets, which sell for 12 x $18.75 = $225. Subtract the cost from the revenue."
  }
